To find the determinant of the given matrix, we can use the Laplace expansion along the first row.

The determinant of the matrix is:

$\det\left(\begin{array}{cccc}
\frac{4}{3} & 1 & -\frac{9}{2} & -\frac{13}{3} \\
-\frac{13}{3} & \frac{25}{6} & -\frac{19}{6} & \frac{11}{6} \\
-\frac{23}{6} & \frac{29}{6} & -\frac{10}{3} & -\frac{19}{6} \\
-\frac{17}{6} & -\frac{7}{6} & \frac{5}{2} & \frac{7}{3}
\end{array}\right) = \frac{4}{3}\left|\begin{array}{ccc}
\frac{25}{6} & -\frac{19}{6} & \frac{11}{6} \\
\frac{29}{6} & -\frac{10}{3} & -\frac{19}{6} \\
-\frac{7}{6} & \frac{5}{2} & \frac{7}{3}
\end{array}\right| - 1\left|\begin{array}{ccc}
-\frac{13}{3} & -\frac{19}{6} & \frac{11}{6} \\
-\frac{23}{6} & -\frac{10}{3} & -\frac{19}{6} \\
-\frac{17}{6} & \frac{5}{2} & \frac{7}{3}
\end{array}\right| + \left(-\frac{9}{2}\right)\left|\begin{array}{ccc}
-\frac{13}{3} & \frac{25}{6} & \frac{11}{6} \\
-\frac{23}{6} & \frac{29}{6} & -\frac{19}{6} \\
-\frac{17}{6} & -\frac{7}{6} & \frac{7}{3}
\end{array}\right| + \left(-\frac{13}{3}\right)\left|\begin{array}{ccc}
-\frac{13}{3} & \frac{25}{6} & -\frac{19}{6} \\
-\frac{23}{6} & \frac{29}{6} & -\frac{10}{3} \\
-\frac{17}{6} & -\frac{7}{6} & \frac{5}{2}
\end{array}\right|$

Simplifying the determinants, we get:

$\det\left(\begin{array}{cccc}
\frac{4}{3} & 1 & -\frac{9}{2} & -\frac{13}{3} \\
-\frac{13}{3} & \frac{25}{6} & -\frac{19}{6} & \frac{11}{6} \\
-\frac{23}{6} & \frac{29}{6} & -\frac{10}{3} & -\frac{19}{6} \\
-\frac{17}{6} & -\frac{7}{6} & \frac{5}{2} & \frac{7}{3}
\end{array}\right) = \frac{4}{3}\left(-\frac{35}{18}\right) - 1\left(\frac{11}{9}\right) + \left(-\frac{9}{2}\right)\left(\frac{19}{18}\right) + \left(-\frac{13}{3}\right)\left(\frac{23}{18}\right)$

Simplifying further, we get:

$\det\left(\begin{array}{cccc}
\frac{4}{3} & 1 & -\frac{9}{2} & -\frac{13}{3} \\
-\frac{13}{3} & \frac{25}{6} & -\frac{19}{6} & \frac{11}{6} \\
-\frac{23}{6} & \frac{29}{6} & -\frac{10}{3} & -\frac{19}{6} \\
-\frac{17}{6} & -\frac{7}{6} & \frac{5}{2} & \frac{7}{3}
\end{array}\right) = \boxed{-\frac{29}{27}}$
